📖 LEARNED: Herbal Medicine (Level 2). You know dosages, preparations, contraindications. This is real medicine, just old.
📖 LEARNED: Reading the Land (Level 2). Edges are the grocery store — where meadow meets woods, where water meets bank. Disturbed ground regrows first and fattest.
📖 LEARNED: The Forager’s Eye (Level 2). Edges, disturbed ground, last year’s growth — you read a hillside like a menu and strip it clean.
📖 Your old life taught you things. 3 skills from your past — check your Journal.
📖 Your hands remember: knap a Stone knife (stone + vine) — the oldest tool there is. Find the stone.
📖 Your hands remember: weave cloth (3 plant fiber — strip it from cleared brush), and build a Water Filter (cloth + charcoal from fire ashes). Dirty water doesn't have to stay dirty.
You wake up with dirt in your mouth and blood on your hands that isn't yours. The sky is the wrong color — not sunset-wrong, wound-wrong. Deirdre Perez. Florist. From Columbus, Ohio. That was yesterday. This is now. You have: Field suture kit, Photo album, Home key, Carpenter's square, Dispatcher's headset. That's everything you own in this world. Haven. Twelve people. The fire is lit. Last night, something walked past the treeline on two legs. Too tall. It stopped. It listened. Then it kept going. Nobody slept after that.
A woman, maybe 40s, with restless hands: "Nothing grows here but dirt and tents. Past the treeline — that's where the green is. That's where the food is."
📓 Journal: Food won't come to Haven. Walk past the treeline — learn what grows out there, bring it back, and get it named at camp.
You tell the others you're heading out. Someone nods. "Come back before dark."
— DAY 1 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active.
